  "version": 1,
  "about": "Nixie 1.9 (Collections 2): TMDb keywords a category rule may match beyond the allowlist and the seasonal keywords (Keywords.cs; \"thanksgiving\" is seasonal since 1.9). Public TMDb keyword names only, lower case, as Jellyfin files them as tags. Matched, never named: no collection, reason line or More like line is ever made of one of these alone. Left out on purpose: production junk (\"duringcreditsstinger\"), spoilers (\"twist ending\", \"death of …\"), sex and harm words, and slurs. Every keyword here is used by a rule in micro-genres.json or in its draft (tools/collections/draft.json): once a release has shipped the list, a change to it means a new index revision (every title read again; LibraryIndex pins the kept keywords' count and hash), so a drafted category brought back needs none. Each keyword has a group; groups say why.",
  "groups": {
    "tone": "TMDb's tone keywords: the only field that backs a mood word in a name (\"Witty\", \"Feel-Good\", \"Suspenseful\")",
    "subgenre": "TMDb's names for subgenres and forms the genre list doesn't separate (\"folk horror\", \"space opera\")",
    "source": "What a film is based on, beside the allowlist's books, comics, manga and true stories",
    "place": "Settings: a city, a landscape or a kind of place",
    "period": "Periods and wars a story is set in (a decade keyword is a setting, not a release date)",
    "crime": "Crime's subjects: the mob, cartels, hitmen, robberies, chases and outlaws",
    "law-politics": "Courts, politics, spies and conspiracies",
    "supernatural": "Creatures, magic, myths and possession, beside the allowlist's ghosts, vampires and werewolves",
    "work": "Jobs and the people a story follows",
    "life": "Family, love, weddings, school, migration, addiction and pets",
    "lgbtq": "LGBTQ+ stories, in TMDb's own words: matched for a rule, never shown as a name",
    "music-sport": "Music, dance, and the sports the allowlist's \"sports\" doesn't split",
    "nature": "Nature, disasters, the sea and treasure"
  },
